@ Index:   Inverse Gudermannian function plot
@ Author:  Jaco Mostert
@ Created: 2026-08-09
@ Version: 5
@ Tested:  Plots the inverse Gudermannian S-curve, range (-1.69, -4.57) to (1.69, 4.57).
@ Input:   None; runs over 101 points
@ Output:  Inverse Gudermannian S-curve, (-1.69, -4.57) to (1.69, 4.57)
@
@ The loop walks 101 points, works each one out from the counter rather than
@ from a stored range, and collects the pairs in the statistics registers.
@
@ TICKS# is read at the start and again at the end, so the program leaves
@ its own run time in X as a string of seconds.
@
@ The plot is drawn by PLSTAT and PLTFCNS once the sweep is finished.
@
@ Clears FRACT and IRFRAC on entry to allow reliable integer division in
@ the counter arithmetic.
LBL ‘GudrmPL’
  LocR 15
  STOS R.00
  RAD
  CF ‘FRACT’
  CF ‘IRFRAC’
  CLΣ
  TICKS#
  STO N
  101
  STO M
  STO O

  LBL :LOOP:
    VIEW M
    RCL O
    RCL- M

    # CALCULATION START
    RCL O
    DECR X
    2
    IDIV
    ÷
    1
    -
    0.49
    ×
    𝜋
    ×
    ENTER
    g_d⁻¹
    𝑥⇄𝑦

    # ENDCALC
    Σ+
    DSZ M
      GTO :LOOP:
    TICKS#
    RCL- N
    10
    ÷
    ‘ sec’
    +
    PLSTAT
    PLTFCNS
  END
